From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add RNNoise's LICENSE at project root

librnnoise.so is built from the xiph/rnnoise git submodule and statically
linked into every pyrnnoise wheel, but setup.py ships no license_files
list and the submodule's own COPYING (BSD-3-Clause) lives outside the
project root, so setuptools' default LICEN[CS]E*/COPYING*/NOTICE*/
AUTHORS* glob never picks it up. Every wheel on PyPI currently ships
only pyrnnoise's own Apache-2.0 LICENSE.

Copy rnnoise/COPYING to the root as LICENSE.rnnoise, which the existing
default glob already matches with no setup.py change.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; needs a pull request against pengzhendong/pyrnnoise]
---
 LICENSE.rnnoise | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 LICENSE.rnnoise

diff --git a/LICENSE.rnnoise b/LICENSE.rnnoise
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..59d7d09
--- /dev/null
+++ b/LICENSE.rnnoise
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
